    "title": "Letters: Cameras for overall safety not invasion of personal privacy - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Rich Nanc Ozga ,\n9 hours ago I was born in Chicago in the mid-1940s and lived there until the early ’70s.\nDuring this period, my family and neighbors throughout the neighborhood never had to nor did lock our doors. Chicago was reasonably safe during this period.\nMy siblings and I walked two to three miles to school and it never had any issues with crime, vandalism, etc. This was primarily due to there being sufficient police to keep our neighborhoods safe.\nNow is another story, primarily due to “citizens” not wanting to provide sufficient funding (taxes) for our own safety - i.e. police or other means.\nPeople that attempt to use the excuse that cameras are an “invasion of privacy” are burying their head in the sand.\nThey don’t want to face reality. It’s either support more funding for police or Flock cameras.",
